13. Graph Database Query Processing using Neo4j
Graph traversal & pattern-based queries
Cypher uses pattern matching:
MATCH (u:User)-[:FRIENDS_WITH]->(f:User)-[:LIKES]->(p:Post)
WHERE u.name = "Alice"
RETURN p
Traversals follow relationships directly (no join tables).
Why more effective than relational joins
Relational joins become expensive with many hops (self-joins on large tables).
Graph engines use index-free adjacency → constant-time hop.
Excellent for path finding, recommendations, community detection on highly connected data.
